r","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record from 1951 to 2025 shows April to May and August to September each came in under 90% of normal in 35 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 9 grids. In 2025 the middle sat at 60% of normal for July to August. So far in 2026, June to July ran 161% of normal on the middle. Every grid had its driest year in 1964, and grid 27225 got just 59% of normal that year.</p>"}
